      "writtenOn": "2026-09-16T09:56:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That sounds exactly why we should be doing it in gerrit? I suspect that most experienced gerrit sites have something similar with no good reason for it being different?",
      "parentUuid": "8803015b_25ba97dc",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31b047d7_819a61f9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003873
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-16T09:59:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On the other hand, everyone does Gerrit monitoring but the whole monitoring setup and infrastructure is not a part of Gerrit itself.",
      "parentUuid": "043ed98d_d445c701",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e962e1d_200be853",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-19T18:10:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Whey do you think this fits if not in gerrit core?",
      "parentUuid": "31b047d7_819a61f9",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e09d3836_18b5972c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003873
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T08:00:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It fits in whatever monitoring system one uses. I mean, Gerrit core exposes the \u0027show-queue\u0027 endpoint both via SSH and REST, so one can periodically fetch that.\n\nIf we let this into Gerrit core then the next thing could be to periodically write java thread dumps into a log, which is also useful for post-incident analysis. Just to give one more example.\n\nBtw, if you really want to emit that log from Gerrit runtime you can also do it from a plugin?",
      "parentUuid": "7e962e1d_200be853",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6f0586d_36de3dea",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T11:02:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thread dumps are risky, as they can slow down/block operations, otherwise I would agree that it WOULD make sense in core! I think that the fact that we have them in the gerrit.sh script already shows that this is something that people feel is fundamental. I believe metrics are mostly in core today? I know there are metrics plugins which interface with external monitoring systems, but this isn\u0027t an interface to an external system like Prometheus, this is effectively an internal system which uses the log system directly, and we write all sorts of logs (including from plugins) already, it is simple and requires very little from an admin.\n\nI personally think this is a very valuable thing to have in core, and I would prefer not to have to setup an external system to do this on all my systems. I would ask you to imagine yourself changing jobs, and still working on Gerrit, would you want to have to configure an external system to do this, or would you prefer to have it just happening for you by Gerrit? I feel this is the type of thing that makes onboarding Gerrit easier (and that we should be making onboarding easier).",
      "parentUuid": "e09d3836_18b5972c",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a5a5e9a_8d5aff74",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003873
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T12:10:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, metrics are in core and, in my opinion, this is same like \"show-queue is in core\". We use plugins to push metrics into an external system (like prometheus).\nBy the same analogy we can use a plugin to push show-queue periodically in an external system (log file or something remote).\n\nI will not actively oppose this change",
      "parentUuid": "b6f0586d_36de3dea",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86893db0_a31aa993",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T16:12:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tl;dr: a plugin seems like a good fit\n\nI don\u0027t have strong opinions on this change and I see both points from Martin and Sasa. I suspect many admins run something like this as an external task and therefore I agree that it would make sense to provide a standard way to do that. The plugin approach seems like a good compromise on those, since I can imagine that different setups would use different export targets (log file, logging collector, etc.). Considering almost all of the added code/content in this change could just move directly to a plugin, that really seems to support that approach.",
      "parentUuid": "7a5a5e9a_8d5aff74",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9d98202_030903c5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T16:16:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern is that this likely doesn\u0027t fit well in an existing plugin, and it doesn\u0027t feel like something which deserves its own plugin either? Does anyone have a good suggestion for a good plugin to put this in?",
      "parentUuid": "86893db0_a31aa993",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a682a955_0de0efaf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T23:48:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked through the options and I don\u0027t think there\u0027s a good existing plugin. Seems like it would be fine in its own plugin, if you can find a good name for it (`queue-reporter-logFile`?). Each of the metrics reporters have a plugin and this does feel very similar. I guess if you could abstract the \"file\" part away, you could make the plugin more generically `-log4j` and then someone can use whatever appender/format/etc they want that works with log4j.",
      "parentUuid": "b9d98202_030903c5",
      "revId": "6eddb134cf97bb5b944872a71a007cdb4f77dfca",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
